100
00:05:55,220 --> 00:06:00,580
A little note about
declarative versus imperative.

101
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:04,795
Each of these are a
different approach.

102
00:06:04,795 --> 00:06:09,485
Imperative is when you say
how to get what you want.

103
00:06:09,485 --> 00:06:14,600
Think of a script that
says create VM 1,

104
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,755
create VM 2,

105
00:06:16,755 --> 00:06:19,555
install this software
package on it.

106
00:06:19,555 --> 00:06:23,115
It's imperative approach,

107
00:06:23,115 --> 00:06:27,375
sequentially describing exactly
how to get what you want.

108
00:06:27,375 --> 00:06:29,770
A declarative approaches where

109
00:06:29,770 --> 00:06:31,910
you just say what you want.

110
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:35,735
You don't say how to
actually go about doing it.

111
00:06:35,735 --> 00:06:38,805
But what it does,

112
00:06:38,805 --> 00:06:42,220
and this is where to
Terraform comes in,

113
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:45,485
is you describe
the desired state

114
00:06:45,485 --> 00:06:49,460
and it will look up what
the current state is,

115
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:53,790
and Terraform runs this
reconciliation loop where it

116
00:06:53,790 --> 00:07:00,485
is doing things that try to
get you to the desired state.

117
00:07:00,485 --> 00:07:09,370
Then if you ever change
the desired state,

118
00:07:09,370 --> 00:07:11,835
say, launch a third VM,

119
00:07:11,835 --> 00:07:13,305
well, it'll look and say,

120
00:07:13,305 --> 00:07:15,180
I only have two VMs created,

121
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:17,620
let me create just
that third one.

122
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:21,420
Or if I accidentally
deleted one,

123
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:24,280
maybe I went through
the portal to delete

124
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:27,260
it and the desired
state is still two,

125
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:28,640
and they'll say, great,

126
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:30,020
I'm supposed to have two,

127
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:34,245
but I only have one, and
it will launch the second.

128
00:07:34,245 --> 00:07:36,270
That's what declarative is.

129
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:41,060
It's quite powerful when
you get used to it.

